    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance measurements. It assumes a cluster of N nodes, each running one or more serving processes (\"ranks\"), coordinated by a scheduler or orchestrator.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every rank is running the same logical system.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must match. Do not rely on \"same path\" \u2014 verify content, since network filesystems and image layers can diverge.\n- [ ] **Code and image version.** Record container image digests (not tags), git commit SHAs, and build timestamps for the serving binary on every rank. Tags are mutable; digests are not.\n- [ ] **Parallelism topology.** Confirm tensor-parallel size (TP), pipeline-parallel size (PP), expert-parallel size (EP), and data-parallel replicas match the intended launch configuration on every rank. Verify TP \u00d7 PP \u00d7 EP \u00d7 DP relationships are internally consistent (e.g., world size = TP \u00d7 PP \u00d7 DP for simple layouts).\n- [ ] **Quantization and dtype.** Verify weight dtype, KV-cache dtype, activation dtype, and any quantization scheme (GPTQ/AWQ/FP8) are identical across ranks. Mixed precision across ranks is a silent correctness bug.\n- [ ] **Sampling parameter defaults.** Confirm default temperature, top-p, top-k, max tokens, and stop conditions are identical across replicas if requests may be routed to any replica.\n- [ ] **Context length and rope settings.** Verify max sequence length, RoPE scaling, and sliding-window settings match across",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
